I'm wondering if anyone here knows what the usage requirements are for
the 16x16 tileset that comes with graphical version of Nethack.

I would assume they are covered by the same licence as the Nethack
source code (which is a modified GPL); but let me draw your attention
to the tiles here:
http://rltiles.sourceforge.net/
Some of those tiles are identical to the tiles used by Nethack, but
the licence on that site is less restrictive. So I'm not sure if
"rltiles" is violating the nethack licence or if the tiles are
available under some less restrictive licence. Maybe the tiles are
made by the same people! I just don't know.

Does anyone know?

The reason I'm asking is that I'm currently working on my own tile-
based game, and I'm starting think about replacing my current
"graphics" (which are just primitive shapes such as triangles and
squares). My game is currently on github with the AGPL licence, which
is probably compatible with the Nethack GPL, but nevertheless I'd like
to properly understand my rights and responsibilities. Maybe I'll
change my mind about my licencing, or maybe the owner of the artwork
will decide they don't want me using it!


